        "candidate_context": "Name: Daniel Okonkwo\nSummary (their own words): Data analyst with 2 years of experience turning operational data into reporting that non-technical managers actually use. Strong SQL and Excel, currently building out Python skills.\nStated years of experience: 2.0\nSkills on CV (13): Data Cleaning, Data Visualisation, Excel, Google Analytics, Pandas, Power BI, Statistics, Tableau, SQL, scikit-learn, Presentation Skills, Stakeholder Management, Python\n\nExperience: Data Analyst at Mercia Retail Group (Jan 2024 - Present)\n  - Responsible for the weekly sales performance pack circulated to regional managers\n  - Worked on cleaning and consolidating point-of-sale data from 48 stores\n  - Built a Power BI dashboard tracking stock availability that replaced a manual spreadsheet process\n  - Investigated a reporting discrepancy and traced it to duplicated records in the nightly load\n\nExperience: Junior Reporting Analyst at Mercia Retail Group (Jul 2023 - Dec 2023)\n  - Produced ad-hoc SQL extracts for the finance and marketing teams\n  - Maintained the existing Excel reporting suite\n  - Documented the definitions behind each KPI so the numbers could be reproduced\n\nProject: Customer Churn Exploration [Python, Pandas, scikit-learn]\n  Analysed a public telecoms churn dataset, compared logistic regression with a decision tree, and wrote up which features mattered most. Reported accuracy of 79% on a held-out test set.\n\nProject: Analysed a public telecoms churn dataset, compared logistic regression with a decision\n  tree, and wrote up which features mattered most. Reported accuracy of 79% on a held-out test set.\n\nProject: Football Attendance Dashboard [Tableau]\n  Built a public dashboard exploring attendance trends across four seasons.\nEducation: BSc, Birmingham, University of Birmingham, 2023\nEducation: BSc Economics, Economics, University of Birmingham, 2023\nCertifications: Google Data Analytics Professional Certificate - Coursera",
        "role_context": "Role summary: Conducts data analysis to provide insights and support decision-making processes.\nCore technical requirements: Python, SQL, Data Visualisation, Excel, Data Warehousing, Tableau, AWS, Communication, Git, Data Structures & Algorithms, Data Cleaning, ETL, Linux, Teamwork, Data Science & Analytics, Documentation\nDesirable: Big Data, Statistics, Power BI, CI/CD, Kubernetes, Docker, Certified Data Analyst (CDA), Jupyter, MongoDB, MySQL\nTools and platforms: AWS, Git, CI/CD, Kubernetes, Docker, Linux, Jupyter, Google Cloud Platform, Jira, Microsoft Azure\nProfessional skills: Communication, Presentation Skills, Project Management, Teamwork, Leadership, Customer Focus, Adaptability, Attention to Detail\nInterview focus areas: Data analysis techniques, Data visualization tools, SQL and data querying, Data storytelling and communication, Project management and team collaboration, Data governance and compliance\nTypical responsibilities: Analyze data to identify trends and patterns, Prepare and present data reports to stakeholders, Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand business needs, Design and implement data pipelines and workflows, Perform data cleaning and preprocessing, Conduct statistical analysis and predictive modeling, Support data governance and compliance initiatives, Train and mentor junior analysts",
